\\ A failing task cancels its sibling (TC1-C1, spec/tc1/CONCURRENCY.md section 7).
\\
\\ The supervisor task opens a scope with two children: a waiter blocked on a
\\ channel nobody sends to, and a worker that divides by zero. The worker's trap
\\ latches into the scope and requests the waiter's cancellation, which removes it
\\ from the channel and is delivered when it next runs; the supervisor's own body
\\ carries on and emits. When the scope joins, its children are done and its latch
\\ is set, so it exits ChildFailed, and so does the supervisor. main sees that
\\ through await. Observing a failure does not acknowledge it: the supervisor's
\\ trap is latched into main's own implicit scope, so main ends ChildFailed too.
\\
\\ Expected:
\\ > emit "supervisor": 0 (task 1)
\\ > emit "failed": ChildFailed (task 0)
\\ > outcome: Trap ChildFailed
\\ > schedule: policy fifo, a production schedule by the model's records

(define main {I64 --> I64}
  input -> (let ch (channel I64 1)
                supervisor (spawn (lambda (_ : Unit)
                             (scope
                               (let waiter (spawn (lambda (_ : Unit)
                                                    (match (receive ch)
                                                      ((Item x) -> x)
                                                      (End -> 0))))
                                    worker (spawn (lambda (_ : Unit) (/ 1 0)))
                                 (do (emit "supervisor" 0) 0)))))
             (match (await supervisor)
               ((Ok v) -> v)
               (Cancelled -> -1)
               ((Failed code) -> (do (emit "failed" code) -2)))))
